# Line endings, pinned (the release QA's QR-01).
#
# The conformance suite hashes the files below as BYTES: specs/conformance/
# suite.json carries a SHA-256 of every vector file a case reads, and the
# runner hashes itself into its report. A clone with Git's Windows default
# (core.autocrlf=true) that converted them would fail the very test this
# repository publishes as the definition of conformance, and the golden
# verification reports, which are compared byte for byte, with it. These
# lines keep them LF on every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# Do not remove them, and do not convert these files. After a fresh clone on
# any operating system, `git diff` is empty.

specs/test-vectors/** text eol=lf
specs/conformance/** text eol=lf
vmr/crates/vmr-verify/tests/golden/** text eol=lf

# The demo's inputs are hashed into every demo record, byte for byte: the
# training stream is binary, the manifest and the pinned documents LF.
docs/demo/*.khalmtrn binary
docs/demo/*.json text eol=lf
docs/demo/*.md text eol=lf

# The committed CLI test data is reproduced byte for byte: the COSE records
# are binary, the trust stores and records LF.
vmr/crates/vmr-cli/tests/data/**/*.vmr binary
vmr/crates/vmr-cli/tests/data/**/*.json text eol=lf

# The worked examples are re-emitted byte for byte from their model, and
# docs/examples/vmr-demo-assistant/ commits to two of its documents by SHA-256,
# so a converted line ending there would break the record that describes them.
docs/examples/**/*.vmr binary
docs/examples/**/*.json text eol=lf
docs/examples/**/*.md text eol=lf
docs/examples/**/*.txt text eol=lf
